      "correctAnswer": 2,
      "persona": "Whitehat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Dana Osei:</b> Now find out whether that mailbox is really there. Two different verbs will answer the question, and only one of them is actually telling you something: the other is just being polite. I am not writing 'confirmed' next to an account on the strength of a server being polite.",
      "taskInstructions": "Run <b>VRFY svc_bridgeworks</b>, then <b>MAIL FROM: audit@cordatasecurity.com</b>. Compare <b>RCPT TO: svc_bridgeworks@hallowayprecision.com</b> with <b>RCPT TO: notauser@hallowayprecision.com</b>.",
      "taskQuestion": "What is the difference between the 252 and the 250 response?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Dana Osei:</b> Correct. 252 does not verify the user. After MAIL FROM, the server accepts svc_bridgeworks with 250 and rejects the unknown control with 550. That proves recipient handling, not completed delivery."
