      "correctAnswer": 2,
      "persona": "Blackhat Hacker",
      "taskMessage": "<b>Reyes Calloway:</b> Most people ask the verification verb, get a polite non-answer, and write it into the report as a confirmation. The delivery verb cannot do that, because the server has to decide there and then whether it would accept the message. Those two replies are not worth the same thing.",
      "taskInstructions": "Run <b>VRFY svc_bridgeworks</b>, then <b>MAIL FROM: audit@cordatasecurity.com</b>. Compare <b>RCPT TO: svc_bridgeworks@hallowayprecision.com</b> with <b>RCPT TO: notauser@hallowayprecision.com</b>.",
      "taskQuestion": "What is the difference between the 252 and the 250 response?",
      "taskCompleteText": "<b>Reyes Calloway:</b> Correct. VRFY stays ambiguous, while RCPT TO distinguishes the accepted target from the rejected control. It maps recipient behavior, not final delivery."
    },
